117-Candidate items: `def-aqft-susy-wilsonian-action`; `prop-aqft-supersymmetric-threshold-matching`; `thm-aqft-wilsonian-superpotential-nonrenormalization` (only with the regulator, field content, gauge invariance, perturbative scope, and chiral/holomorphic definitions of the selected source); and `ex-aqft-soft-breaking-effective-operator`. Weinberg's perturbative theorem is a candidate source for the nonrenormalization obligation: it allows arbitrary gauge-invariant holomorphic `F(Phi,W)` in the Wilsonian Lagrangian, apart from one-loop gauge-coupling renormalization, subject to a cutoff preserving supersymmetry and gauge invariance. It is not a claim about nonperturbative corrections, arbitrary 1PI actions, or a model-independent absence of all running. Use the physical BPS bridge only after the localization/BPS researcher establishes it; the existing mathematical CoHA contract explicitly demands an additional dictionary and proves no physical index identity.
