+# Batch 17 authoring notes — Wilson Coefficients and Finite-Dimensional RG Systems
+
+## Scope, plan comparison, and inventory
+
+Owned pair: `qftx-eft-rg-data` / `qftx-eft-rg-data-examples`, category and
+library `quantum-field-theory-mathematics` / `mathematics`, order 973. The
+canonical plan row agrees with the design on page identity, title, companion,
+category, library, order, and the three required pages. The canonical row and
+batch manifest currently have empty `items` arrays; these are placeholders.
+The design assigns `def-aqft-scheme-and-wilson-coefficients` and
+`thm-aqft-truncated-coupled-rge-wellposedness` to A. Following the binding
+owner direction, B will contain a worked example authored for this pair.
+
+The item-level contract for the scheme definition originally has no
+`proposed_deps`, although its data are coordinates on the finite local-operator
+quotient and use the local operator engineering dimensions. The assigned design
+requires that finite quotient and dimension interface. The authoring therefore
+declares direct conditional dependencies on
+`def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension` and
+`def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`; this makes the coefficient-space input
+explicit instead of treating the missing operator quotient as already
+constructed. The proposed quotient contract carries full AC from its
+reductive/Reynolds chain, so the new consumers state and declare full AC. This
+dependency correction is recorded here and in the per-edge cross-batch file.
+
+The scale-cocycle candidate links in the inventory are marked nonlogical, and
+the specialist note says they do not supply a general EFT beta function. They
+remain page-level context through `requires`; the new item proofs do not use
+the scalar formal cocycle as a logical premise. The RGE theorem directly uses
+the actual published Picard–Lindelöf theorem after matching its hypotheses.
+
+Item dependency levels, computed before authoring from the in-run item graph:
+
+- `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension`: 0; no in-run item supplier.
+- `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`: planned level 1 from the local-operator
+  definition.
+- `def-aqft-scheme-and-wilson-coefficients`: 2, one plus the maximum level 1
+  of its two direct in-run suppliers.
+- `thm-aqft-truncated-coupled-rge-wellposedness`: 3, one plus the scheme
+  definition's level 2.
+- `ex-aqft-coupled-rge-linear-mixing`: 4, one plus the theorem's level 3.
+
+The batch dependency-level record remains batch 17 at level 2 with batch 16 as
+its page-level supplier. No shared plan or other batch manifest is edited.
+
+## Supplier inspection and unresolved interfaces
+
+- `qftx-eft-operator-quotients` is assigned to batch 16, but its current
+  manifest has no item inventory and its canonical A-page carrier is absent.
+  The planned design says finite-dimensional local operators and a fixed-order
+  quotient by the stated relations. `proposed-inventory.json` names
+  `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension` and
+  `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`, but no complete current statements or
+  proofs are available. The new scheme definition and its consumers use this
+  only as the explicit conditional finite quotient/basis input; they do not
+  claim it has been constructed or proved. The exact in-run item and page
+  carriers must be checked against this recorded use when available.
+- Before treating the missing supplier as a gap, checked current Step-1
+  readiness with `loadStep1Record` and `step1Decision` from
+  `tools/physics-support/frontier-snapshot.mjs` and
+  `tools/physics-support/step1-decisions.mjs`. Its local operator and quotient
+  items have no current carriers or readiness records. This is a carrier gap,
+  not an inference from a missing approval stamp.
+- The proposed quotient's transitive external candidates are
+  `thm-complete-reducibility-and-reynolds-operator-for-complex-reductive-group`,
+  `lem-reynolds-operator-and-invariant-subring-properties`, and
+  `thm-invariant-ring-finite-generation-and-affine-categorical-quotient`.
+  Their complete current statements and proof arguments were read. The first
+  states its full-AC hypothesis and uses AC in its sum-of-simples bridge; the
+  Reynolds lemma inherits AC and its ideal computations themselves use no new
+  choice; the invariant-ring theorem is for commutative affine algebraic
+  actions of complex reductive groups and also assumes AC. Those exact results
+  do not by themselves prove the EFT-specific quotient for arbitrary
+  Grassmann-graded operator spaces, IBP/EOM relations, or field redefinitions.
+  The missing local item must supply that bridge or state its exact narrower
+  input. These transitive observations belong here, not as unowned cross-batch
+  review rows.
+- The current published `qftx-scale-cocycles` page and its two cited item
+  carriers were read in full. Their raw hashes match the current supplier-use
+  inventory. The definition carries Countable Choice, and the proposition
+  proves the twisted formal cocycle by the stated uniqueness result. Its actual
+  scope is formal scalar time-ordered systems and a prescribed one-coupling
+  example; it does not calculate an EFT beta function. This batch does not use
+  it as a logical premise. The missing Step-1 records do not override these
+  complete current proofs or their published status.
+- The pinned `thm-picard-lindelof-local-existence-and-uniqueness` carrier and
+  its two ODE definitions were read in full. The theorem assumes a continuous
+  finite-dimensional vector field, locally Lipschitz in the state variable
+  uniformly on compact cylinders, and proves local existence and uniqueness;
+  its quantitative cylinder clause supplies a common local interval. The
+  imported item hash matches `research/math-imports.json`. The new theorem adds
+  a local continuous-dependence estimate by a complete integral-inequality
+  argument; it asserts no global solution or QFT coefficient calculation.
+- `step1Decision` reports no Step-1 records for the external published ODE and
+  scale items. Their current statements/proofs and, for the ODE theorem, the
+  immutable import pin were inspected directly. Missing readiness alone is not
+  treated as a defect.
+
+## Source research
+
+Four full texts were inspected for this A page: two independent EFT treatments
+and two independent ODE treatments, including the full Teschl book and full
+ODE lecture notes. Exact URLs, locators, read extents, supported items,
+limitations, searches, and per-result dispositions are in
+`advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-17.coverage.json`.
+`source-fetch-check --stamp` is running for those four full-text URLs; its
+actual fetch stamps and result will be recorded after the command completes.
+
+## Authoring and validation checkpoint
+
+No batch 17 item or page carrier existed at the initial inspection. The next
+actions are to author the definition before its theorem, author the B example,
+then finish the manifest, proof contracts, coverage, notes, and cross-batch
+edge records. The definition, theorem, and example remain conditional on the
+exact current batch 16 quotient/dimension inputs. Their Step-1 dispositions
+must therefore remain `escalated` unless those actual carriers become
+available and match the recorded use before readiness is recorded.

