        },
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Assume full AC. Use four-dimensional natural units $c=\\hbar=1$ and a finite jet-polynomial field model with its declared finite rational action of a complex reductive affine algebraic group $G$. Let $W_D$ be a finite raw local-polynomial space at fixed engineering weight $D$, derivative cutoff, and field-degree cutoff; let $V_D=W_D^G$. Let $\\widetilde R_D$ be the $G$-stable linear span in $W_D$ of the declared polynomial identities, admitted total-divergence densities, and leading-equation densities $F^a\\mathcal E_a^{(0)}$ defined below, with $R_D=\\widetilde R_D\\cap V_D$. The finite-order invariant operator quotient is $\\mathcal Q_D=V_D/R_D$.\n\nLet $M=\\mathbb R^{1,3}$ with $x^0=ct$, $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, and volume measure $d^4x$. Even field components are smooth maps $M\\to\\Phi_a^{\\bar0}$ and odd components are smooth coefficient families in a fixed Grassmann algebra valued in $\\Phi_a^{\\bar1}$; admitted variations and currents have compact support. Let $\\mathcal I[L]=\\int_M L\\,d^4x$ on admitted local densities, with the boundary convention $\\mathcal I(\\partial_\\mu J^\\mu)=0$. Let $S_0[\\phi]$ and each $S_j[\\phi]$ be $G$-invariant local polynomial functionals of these field configurations, so their formal Taylor expansions through order $N$ are defined. Let the variational derivative $\\mathcal E_a^{(0)}[\\phi]$ of $S_0$ be defined by\n\n$$\nD S_0[\\phi](h)=\\mathcal I\\!\\left(\\sum_a h^a\\mathcal E_a^{(0)}[\\phi]\\right)\n$$\n\nfor every admitted compactly supported parity-compatible variation $h$. A leading-equation relation is a density $F^a\\mathcal E_a^{(0)}$ with local, compact-support-preserving, parity-compatible $G$-equivariant $F^a[\\phi]$ for which this density lies in $W_D$; an integration-by-parts relation is a density $\\partial_\\mu J^\\mu$ satisfying the stated boundary convention. Consider a finite formal action $S_\\epsilon=S_0+\\sum_{j=1}^N\\epsilon^jS_j$ in the ring $\\mathbb C[\\epsilon]/(\\epsilon^{N+1})$, where $\\epsilon$ is dimensionless and each $\\epsilon^kF^a$ has the units of $\\phi^a$. For every $1\\leq k\\leq N$, the local identity-leading change of variables $\\Psi_k(\\phi)=\\phi-\\epsilon^kF[\\phi]$ is invertible as a formal map through order $N$ and satisfies\n\n$$\nS_\\epsilon[\\Psi_k(\\phi)]=S_\\epsilon[\\phi]-\\epsilon^k\\mathcal I\\!\\left(F^a\\mathcal E_a^{(0)}[\\phi]\\right)+O(\\epsilon^{k+1}).\n$$\n\nThus a coefficient $+\\epsilon^k\\mathcal I(F^a\\mathcal E_a^{(0)})$ can be removed at order $k$ without changing lower-order coefficients, provided all induced terms through the retained order are kept. The quotient $\\mathcal Q_D$ identifies exactly the declared polynomial, boundary, and leading-equation relation span; it asserts no equivalence of arbitrary off-shell Green functions and does not by itself assert a quantum measure or amplitude equivalence.",
