        },
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Let $M=\\mathbb R^{1,3}$ with $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ and natural units $c=\\hbar=1$. Take the trivial symmetry group, one real smooth scalar field $\\phi$ of engineering dimension one with compact support, a mass parameter $m\\geq0$, real dimensionless couplings $g,C$, a cutoff $\\Lambda>0$ of mass dimension one, and a dimensionless formal parameter $\\epsilon$ with $\\epsilon^2=0$. Define $\\mathcal I[f]=\\int_M f\\,d^4x$ for compactly supported densities and use its no-boundary convention $\\mathcal I(\\partial_\\mu J^\\mu)=0$ for compactly supported currents. Set $\\Box=\\eta^{\\mu\\nu}\\partial_\\mu\\partial_\\nu$ and\n\n$$\nS_0[\\phi]=\\mathcal I\\!\\left[-\\frac12\\partial_\\mu\\phi\\,\\partial^\\mu\\phi-\\frac12m^2\\phi^2-\\frac{g}{4!}\\phi^4\\right],\\qquad \\mathcal O_6=\\phi^2\\partial_\\mu\\phi\\,\\partial^\\mu\\phi,\n$$\n\nand the first-order action $S_\\epsilon=S_0+\\epsilon(C/\\Lambda^2)\\mathcal I(\\mathcal O_6)$. Put $\\mathcal E_0=\\Box\\phi-m^2\\phi-(g/6)\\phi^3$, the leading variational derivative to be verified below, and use the relation subspace generated by total divergences and $\\phi^3\\mathcal E_0$. In the finite space with derivative cutoff two, field-degree cutoff six, and engineering weight six, the invariant quotient class is\n\n$$\n[\\mathcal O_6]= -\\frac{m^2}{3}[\\phi^4]-\\frac{g}{18}[\\phi^6].\n$$\n\nThe local map $\\phi\\mapsto\\phi+\\epsilon C\\phi^3/(3\\Lambda^2)$ removes the $\\mathcal O_6$ term at order $\\Lambda^{-2}$ and induces the displayed quartic and sextic coefficient shifts. This is a formal mathematical scalar action example under the stated boundary convention; it does not assert a physical realization or an on-shell scattering result.",
